  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Budget",
      "items": [
        "Default routing budget 10000 ms (routingTimeoutMs)",
        "Dual-backend: Laya gets floor(remaining × ¾) — 7500 ms at defaults, reserving a quarter for Jev",
        "Sole backend gets the full remaining budget",
        "A sole-backend timeout also fails closed",
        "Cancellation: SIGINT exits 130, SIGTERM exits 143"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Fail-closed",
      "items": [
        "No valid choice within budget → no worker, no retry",
        "Rejection before classification emits no receipt",
        "Exactly one turnhelm.receipt once classification starts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Worker safety",
      "items": [
        "At most one Codex worker per run, inside a fresh per-run CODEX_HOME (--ephemeral, --ignore-user-config, --ignore-rules); no discoverable credential means refusal before classification",
        "Sandbox read-only unless --write; --output-schema stages validated bytes inside the managed home — the caller's path is never forwarded",
        "Child env strips credentials; ZDOTDIR redirects to the managed root; TURNHELM_MANAGED_CHILD=1 blocks recursion",
        "--lifecycle records a content-free timeline — first 8 + last 56 of 64 events, overflow marked — on the receipt and best-effort in .turnhelm/lifecycle.jsonl",
        "Stdout carries at most one message — the final agent message of a completed run, classified at emission as strict, extracted (inert trailer dropped, trailerBytes recorded), conflict, or unstructured; no write starts once failure or cancellation is observed (delivery is not transactional)"
      ]
    }
